        "c2pa.ingredients.<i>.title",
        "c2pa.ingredients.<i>.format",
        "c2pa.ingredients.<i>.relationship",
        "c2pa.ai_generated"
      ],
      "notes": "Level-A (parse-only) C2PA / ISO 22144 content provenance. JUMBF (ISO 19566-5) byte streams arrive via PNG `caBX` chunks, JPEG APP11 segments (multi-segment reassembly happens inside `xifty-container-jpeg`), and ISOBMFF `uuid` boxes carrying the C2PA UUID. `c2pa.signature.verified` is always emitted as the string `\"unknown\"` at level A; level B (cryptographic verification) will populate `\"verified\" | \"invalid\" | \"untrusted\"` without a schema bump."
    },
